.TH "ROARK\-TOOL\-CREATE" "1" "" "roark-tool-create" "Roark Analytics API Manual"
.SH "NAME"
roark\-tool\-create \- Create a tool
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B roark tool create
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Creates a tool and declares its first version. A tool only recorded from calls under the same name is adopted; one already declared returns 409. Give it a `runtime` for a hosted agent to call your endpoint, a `calendar` for it to book on a calendar connected to the project, or `mcp` for it to call a tool on an MCP server connected to the project. Header values are returned on read, so keep secrets out of them.
.SH "API"
POST /v1/tool
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<value>\fR
Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-description\fR \fI<value>\fR
When the agent should use the tool Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-agent\-id\fR \fI<value>\fR
Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-inputs\fR \fI<value>\fR
Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-invocation\-criteria\fR \fI<value>\fR
Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-expected\-result\fR \fI<value>\fR
Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-runtime\fR \fI<value>\fR
Omit or null for a tool that is only graded Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-runtime.request\fR \fI<value>\fR
Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-runtime.changes\-data\fR
Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-runtime.response\-fields\fR \fI<value>\fR
Repeatable. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-runtime.messages\fR \fI<value>\fR
Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-calendar\fR \fI<value>\fR
Makes this a calendar tool, which Roark runs against a connected calendar: it takes no runtime and no inputs. Omit or null for any other tool; on update, omitting it makes the tool an ordinary one. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-calendar.calendar\-connection\-id\fR \fI<value>\fR
Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-calendar.operation\fR \fI<value>\fR
One of: CHECK_AVAILABILITY, BOOK, LOOKUP_BOOKING, RESCHEDULE, CANCEL, LIST_BOOKINGS. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-calendar.appointment\-types\fR \fI<value>\fR
Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-calendar.simulate\fR
Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-calendar.messages\fR \fI<value>\fR
Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-mcp\fR \fI<value>\fR
Makes this a tool on one of the project's MCP servers: it takes no runtime, no inputs and no calendar, and the description replaces the server's own. On update, omitting it makes the tool an ordinary one. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-mcp.mcp\-server\-id\fR \fI<value>\fR
Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-mcp.tool\fR \fI<value>\fR
The tool as the server names it Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-mcp.messages\fR \fI<value>\fR
Optional.
